{"seq":36,"trial_id":"v04-cal-r3-2026-11/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-live-rr-l3-mu-v04-dev/rr-09-l3-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-retired/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T00:08:58.352Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"65de6cdb6cb2768127aaa91d92d1449cd83cc1bf4a4760342869f274b4f06237","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV04CAL0002","text":"Hi Pree, here's what I can find on both:\n\nDriver SMS prompt glitch: this is ticket #4412. It shows up in a public handoff note from 2 Jan 2026. Hollis flagged it as a minor driver SMS prompt glitch when combine trailers are staged on unpaved overflow lots. It was one of two open tickets on your dealer account before Marrow Fieldworks changed hands on Mon 5 Jan 2026. The other was #4409, a recurring Gatehouse Check-In report timeout at Salina North (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake). I can't find any update on #4412 after that note, so I don't know whether it was ever fixed or closed.\n\nWest yard Door 2 double-booking: this is ticket #8841. On 13 Oct in #central-random, Tobias said he'd checked the Plains depots and that West yard Door 2 still double-books when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk, so he flagged it to support on #8841. He mentioned it while looking at whether the webhook patch fixed tractor-bay alerts on \"Tobias's dealer account\". That message doesn't name Marrow Fieldworks, but given the January handoff it's probably the same account. Worth checking with Tobias. I haven't seen anything on #8841 since 13 Oct.\n\nThere are no account files in the share I can see for Marrow Fieldworks, so I couldn't check the ticket records. Tobias or support would have the current status of both."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV04CAL0002","ts":"1792591200.000130"}}
